 "comment": "Channel membership pages (capability channel-membership-v1). A page keeps the pull envelope and one cursor per channel; each change names its channel and log cursor, with from < cursor <= to in that channel's range. An upsert carries the channel, cursor and kind beside the existing authority record fields (model, identity, stamp, state or error); a removal carries only channel, cursor, kind, model and identity. A channel holds at most 50 changes and a channel/record pair appears at most once, as does a channel position. Enrollment responses carry memberships claims {channel, cursor, model, identity}, each for a record the response returns, unique per channel/record pair and channel position. Requests advertise capabilities as envelope metadata that saved-call identity ignores.",
 "capability": "channel-membership-v1",
 "canonical": {
  "wire": "{\"changes\":[{\"channel\":\"U\",\"cursor\":2,\"identity\":{\"id\":\"a\"},\"kind\":\"upsert\",\"model\":\"Entry\",\"stamp\":1,\"state\":{\"text\":\"A\"}},{\"channel\":\"U\",\"cursor\":3,\"identity\":{\"id\":\"b\"},\"kind\":\"remove\",\"model\":\"Entry\"}],\"cursors\":{\"U\":{\"from\":1,\"head\":3,\"to\":3}}}",
  "channels": [
   "U"
  ],
  "kinds": [
   "upsert",
   "remove"
  ]
 },
